Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-10-2000||12:05 AM||||I realize it puts strain on the car, but I just have this uncontrollable urge to roast my Fiero's tires from a dead stop, but I can't!  It's an auto!  I even have the performance axle ratio according to the RPO codes, but I still can't even chirp them!  roooooaaaarrrr!  I need to buy another manual Fiero!!!!!  Doesn't anybody else feel my pain?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||01-10-2000||12:18 AM||||You can put a line lock on the front brakes and spin till the tires pop.  Or you can take a windshield washer pump and run hoses to the rear tires and rig it to squirt the tire with soapy water. (hummm)||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||01-10-2000||01:43 AM||||Better yet put VHT in the squiter. Its what they use at the track. Its slippery at first then as it heats up get sticky. Makes blue smoke too||||reg||1
Z||000003||kong||01-10-2000||03:02 AM||||If you really want to make em smoke do it like they do in the movies. Rig up the little squiter and fill it with WD40. You'll be able to smoke em for a block. Just be carefull the tires will get real slippery, and don't wreck the car while you're doing it!<p>[This message has been edited by kong (edited 01-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-10-2000||05:06 AM||||We used to use bleach when I was younger.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||01-10-2000||11:01 AM||||I don't do it with my 86 GT, but we used to use raw horsepower out of a big block.  I do miss that 4-8 miles per gallon fun.  My brother had a car I used to get to change motor and tranny mounts on a lot. A 70 RT w\440 6-pack on it. What a beast! with no NOS it put out about 600 horse.  It was tough not to smoke them off in any gear.  WE couldn't fit bigger tires without tubing the wells out.  Oh well, memories <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||2birds||01-10-2000||01:20 PM||||I'm reluctant to try it with my 86 GT.  My clutches have only lasted 60,000 miles anyway.  I had a 52 Ford pickup back in my high school days, with a 4bbl 390/C-6.  The stock rear end had 4.27 gears so I could light it up at will.  It was fun until the ring and pinion launched.  Torque rules!!!||||reg||6
